You are executing the saas-tenant-lifecycle-runbook skill. Mandate: produce Tenant_Lifecycle_Runbook.md and a per-stage playbook set covering provisioning, tier change, suspension, reactivation, offboarding, data export, hard delete, and retention.

1. Read Multi_Tenancy_Architecture_Spec.md, Runbook.md, Compliance_Docs.md, billing & metering spec, DPA / privacy obligations. Log all paths. Halt if Multi_Tenancy_Architecture_Spec.md is missing.
2. Build the tenant-lifecycle event catalogue table (Event | Trigger | Source service | Downstream consumers | SLA). Include at minimum: tenant.created, tenant.tier_changed, tenant.suspended, tenant.reactivated, tenant.offboarded, tenant.export_requested, tenant.hard_deleted.
3. For each event, generate a playbooks/NN-<stage>.md file. Every playbook MUST contain: Trigger, Pre-conditions, Actor, Automated steps (ordered list), Manual gates, Per-service propagation (table: service | required action), Verification (post-conditions and how tested), Rollback / abort, Audit-trail entry (what + where + retention), Customer-comms message (subject + body + in-app banner if applicable), Retention-policy reference (link to compliance doc).
4. The provisioning playbook MUST cover idempotency, tier-aware resource fan-out, identity bootstrap, cost-estimate snapshot, welcome workflow enqueue.
5. The suspension playbook MUST cover trigger classes (billing past due, compliance breach, admin security), pre-comms, gateway block, audit, tenant-visible UX, reactivation path.
6. The offboarding + data-export + hard-delete playbooks MUST cover: soft-delete grace period, customer-initiated export with format/delivery/auth/audit, hard-delete enumeration of every data store (primary DB, replicas, backups, search index, cache, object storage, log archives), zero-row verification query, destruction certificate, legal-hold pre-condition, backup-retention disclosure.
7. Write Tenant_Lifecycle_Runbook.md with sections: 1) Event Catalogue, 2) Per-Stage Playbook Index, 3) Audit-Trail Destinations, 4) Retention Obligations per Region and Data Class, 5) Customer-Comms Templates, 6) Legal-Hold Procedure, 7) Cross-References to DPA / Privacy Doc Set.

Validation: Halt if any event lacks a playbook. Halt if any playbook lacks Verification, Audit-trail, Customer-comms, or Retention reference. Halt if hard-delete playbook lacks the verification query or the destruction certificate.
